{
  "rationale": "Use a small sensor plant plus a motion-capability plant, then layer compact specifications that map sensed obstacle conditions to exactly one safe recovery action and otherwise bias toward forward exploration. Open-loop pulse semantics are handled by making action states one-shot and by self-looping non-critical path_clear in commit states while allowing obstacle events to preempt for safety.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensing and actuation into plant automata, then encode policy in specifications",
    "Prefer move_forward in clear conditions, use random_walk only as a secondary exploration mode, use directed turns for side/front obstacles, reserve move_backward only for front-obstacle recovery, and reserve full_rotate only after repeated blocked-front failures"
  ],
